  "titles": {
    "_tiers_note": "Akkadian backbone, ascending; the imperial tier blends in the Egyptian overlay: Shar-Per (king of the Great House) over the Per-Sharrutu. -u/-utu rhyme the lower native tiers (Hazannu/Hazannutu ... Sharru/Sharrutu). Hazannu (mayor) barony; Massaru (warden) march; Shaknu (governor) county; Turtanu (commander) duchy; Rubu (prince) principality. DISPLAY titles are English, except the kingdom tier shows the approved foreign throne-term Pharaoh (the Egyptian-overlay kingship; the native form remains Sharru, the v1 empire tier was Shar-Per). (Rank titles are the real Akkadian/Egyptian register, allowed.)",
    "approved_foreign_terms_used": [
      "Pharaoh (kingdom)"
    ],
    "display_policy": "Ruler/domain titles shown in setting-gen, domain lists and vassal trees are ENGLISH (or an approved commonly-known foreign term where set in 'ruler'). The *_native conlang forms are for NPC DIALOGUE ONLY, never for structural/UI displays.",
